# Deep Learning · Autoencoders (PDF, page numbers stored)
{"id":"ae-architecture","resourceId":"cmowjxpqf000004l495c284q8","question":"What are the three components of an autoencoder's basic architecture?","expectedPages":[3],"evidence":["Latent Space : compressed representation"],"referenceAnswer":"An encoder (x to z), a latent space holding the compressed representation, and a decoder (z to x)."}
{"id":"ae-loss","resourceId":"cmowjxpqf000004l495c284q8","question":"Which loss functions are commonly used to train an autoencoder, and for what kind of data?","expectedPages":[8],"evidence":["MSE → continuous data","Binary Cross Entropy → binary data"],"referenceAnswer":"Mean squared error for continuous data and binary cross-entropy for binary data, both minimising reconstruction error."}
{"id":"ae-bottleneck","resourceId":"cmowjxpqf000004l495c284q8","question":"why cant an autoencoder just copy its input straight to the output","expectedPages":[9],"evidence":["Cannot memorize everything due to bottleneck"],"referenceAnswer":"The bottleneck latent layer is too small to memorise everything, so reconstruction forces it to learn compressed features."}
{"id":"ae-sparse-rho","resourceId":"cmowjxpqf000004l495c284q8","question":"In a sparse autoencoder, what does rho represent and what is a typical value?","expectedPages":[18],"evidence":["desired sparsity level (small value, e.g., 0.05)"],"referenceAnswer":"Rho is the desired sparsity level (average activation), a small value such as 0.05."}
{"id":"ae-denoising-loss","resourceId":"cmowjxpqf000004l495c284q8","question":"When training a denoising autoencoder, is the loss computed against the noisy input or the clean input?","expectedPages":[22,23],"evidence":["Compare clean input and reconstructed output"],"referenceAnswer":"Against the original clean input: the reconstruction is compared with x, not with the noisy x-tilde."}
{"id":"ae-vae-reparam","resourceId":"cmowjxpqf000004l495c284q8","question":"What is the reparameterization trick in a variational autoencoder?","expectedPages":[32],"evidence":["Reparameterization trick"],"referenceAnswer":"The latent vector is sampled as z = mu + sigma * epsilon, so sampling stays differentiable."}
{"id":"ae-vs-pca","resourceId":"cmowjxpqf000004l495c284q8","question":"Why are autoencoders better than PCA for dimensionality reduction?","expectedPages":[36,35],"evidence":["PCA learns linear relationships","Alternative to PCA with nonlinear capability"],"referenceAnswer":"PCA only captures linear relationships; autoencoders learn nonlinear ones, which works better for images, speech and text."}
{"id":"ae-anomaly","resourceId":"cmowjxpqf000004l495c284q8","question":"how can autoencoders catch fraud or weird network traffic","expectedPages":[38,35],"evidence":["Large error → Anomaly","Detects unusual patterns using reconstruction error"],"referenceAnswer":"Train only on normal data; at test time a large reconstruction error marks the input as an anomaly."}
{"id":"ae-784-bottleneck","resourceId":"cmowjxpqf000004l495c284q8","question":"In the dimensionality reduction example, how many neurons does the bottleneck have for a 784-pixel image?","expectedPages":[36,5],"evidence":["784 → 256 → 64 → 32 neurons"],"referenceAnswer":"32 neurons (784 → 256 → 64 → 32)."}

# Deep Learning · RNN (PDF, page numbers stored)
{"id":"rnn-why","resourceId":"cmowk10lt000104l4w1bhynef","question":"Why do we need recurrent neural networks instead of a normal feed-forward network?","expectedPages":[3],"evidence":["Traditional neural network limitation: no memory"],"referenceAnswer":"Feed-forward networks assume independent inputs and have no memory; RNNs handle sequence dependency."}
{"id":"rnn-elman","resourceId":"cmowk10lt000104l4w1bhynef","question":"What is a vanilla RNN also called, and who is it named after?","expectedPages":[12],"evidence":["Elman RNN"],"referenceAnswer":"An Elman RNN, after Prof. Jeffrey Elman."}
{"id":"rnn-many-to-one","resourceId":"cmowk10lt000104l4w1bhynef","question":"Give examples of tasks that use a many-to-one RNN.","expectedPages":[25,22],"evidence":["Sentiment analysis • Spam detection"],"referenceAnswer":"Sentiment analysis, spam detection and emotion detection: the model reads the whole sequence before predicting."}
{"id":"rnn-bptt","resourceId":"cmowk10lt000104l4w1bhynef","question":"How is an RNN trained?","expectedPages":[36,37],"evidence":["Backpropagation Through Time"],"referenceAnswer":"With backpropagation through time: loss is summed over time steps and gradients flow back through the sequence to update shared weights."}
{"id":"rnn-long-term","resourceId":"cmowk10lt000104l4w1bhynef","question":"Why can't a vanilla RNN learn long-term dependencies?","expectedPages":[39,40],"evidence":["Model forgets early inputs"],"referenceAnswer":"Vanishing gradients make it forget early inputs (and exploding gradients make training unstable)."}
{"id":"rnn-lstm-gates","resourceId":"cmowk10lt000104l4w1bhynef","question":"What are the three gates in an LSTM?","expectedPages":[42],"evidence":["Forget gate • Input gate • Output gate"],"referenceAnswer":"Forget gate, input gate and output gate."}
{"id":"rnn-gru-vs-lstm","resourceId":"cmowk10lt000104l4w1bhynef","question":"How many gates does a GRU have compared to an LSTM, and which one trains faster?","expectedPages":[52],"evidence":["Training speed Slower Faster"],"referenceAnswer":"GRU has 2 gates vs 3 for LSTM, fewer parameters, and trains faster."}
{"id":"rnn-bidirectional","resourceId":"cmowk10lt000104l4w1bhynef","question":"how can a model use words that come later in a sentence to understand an earlier word","expectedPages":[53],"evidence":["Uses past + future context"],"referenceAnswer":"A bidirectional RNN runs a forward and a backward pass, using past and future context."}
{"id":"rnn-attention","resourceId":"cmowk10lt000104l4w1bhynef","question":"What problem of RNNs does the attention mechanism solve?","expectedPages":[58,57],"evidence":["All info → single vector"],"referenceAnswer":"The bottleneck of squeezing the whole sequence into one vector; attention focuses dynamically on the relevant inputs."}

